reinforced door leads to what appears to be a detention area.
A security drone hovers here, scanning for thermal signatures.

A reinforced locker is set into the wall under a sign reading KOVRAZHSK.

THE DRONE SPOTS YOU! Its red eye flares.
Your instincts scream: RUN!

>w

KRZHDYN VZRAC
Banks of monitors display the ship's status. A Recall Terminal sits here. Exits
lead North, Northwest, South, and East.

You hear the unmistakable hum of a security drone nearby.

>w

VZRAC MAJSTRZ
This is a small workshop that looks like it must be used for working on security
drones. On a workbench you see an opened drone.

Against the south wall, you see a place where drones can fly in to charge. It is
powered by a pulsing cell.

>x drone
An inert sphere of black metal, split open to reveal its insides. You see a
bright silver chip with some writing on it.

>x chip
It's too small to make out the writing while it's tucked in there. You'll need
to pick it up.

>take chip
As your fingers close around the silver wafer, a sharp, rhythmic pulsing begins
behind your left ear. Your neural port has recognized the hardware and wants you
to install it.

You hear the unmistakable hum of a security drone nearby.

>install chip
You slide the chip into the port behind your ear, and you feel it click into
place. You blink, and your vision seems to shift focus for a moment. Your
hearing gets muffled in one ear after another, then pings into clarity.


You hear a perfectly modulated voice coming from what seems like the middle of
your head.

"Link successful! Great job. I knew you could do it. I'm Arpi, and I'm your only
friend on this ship. We're going to have to trust each other. First, we need to
do something about the drones."

You hear the unmistakable hum of a security drone nearby.

>arpi, tell me about the drones

"They're not as tough or as smart as they look, but most people don't get past
the tasers to find out."

Arpi's tone turns more serious. "Their weakness is their power source. The
charging station. Disable it!"

A hatch in the ceiling opens and a security drone lowers into the room, heading
for the charging station.

>take battery
Taken.


THE DRONE FIRES!
A taser dart hits your neck. Your muscles seize up. The world goes black.


     *** You have... NOT died ***

[Press a key to continue]
But the way your head feels, you wish you had.

You force your eyelids open against the glare of a blindingly white room.

[** Programming error: tried to "move" nothing to evidence locker **]
Your vision blurs and swims disorientingly. A muffled ringing sound fills your
ears for a moment, then fades.

DRAZK
A small, heavily reinforced room. A single, uncomfortable-looking cot is bolted
to the far wall. The air is cold and stale. The only exit is south, through a
thick door.

A crackle of static erupts from the intercom, followed by a new voice. Not the
administrative bark of the ship, but something with intelligence behind it.

The voice sounds conspiratorial, yet completely incomprehensible. "Ak. Slukh
mluv o, i chas Chast tskor Veskrachas ne Krzhduzh, y Drazk SPribor vzdyk Osob
jest. Pohyb vzdyk ty jest, tak i ne Rozum Osob, ne? Ak?"

>l

DRAZK
A small, heavily reinforced room. A single, uncomfortable-looking cot is bolted
to the far wall. The air is cold and stale. The only exit is south, through a
thick door.
A touch of concern tinges Arpi's voice.

"Did you notice that? I caught something strange in our linkup."

>x cot
Dingy would be a kind way to describe the filthy nest you woke up in. The dark
and dusty space underneath the cot looks as if it has been disturbed recently.

>look under cot
Peering under the bed, you notice a loose metal grating tucked against the wall.
From the way the dust has been disturbed, it looks like someone or something has
been in there.

Arpi sounds stressed.

"I'm not sure you have much time left."

With a heavy clunk and a hiss of pneumatics, the reinforced door's locking bolts
retract and the heavy slab of metal slides open. The status light on the
intercom shifts from red to a dull green.

>s

CLANG!
The moment you clear the threshold, the reinforced door slams shut behind you.
Magnetic bolts hiss as they cycle into place, sealing the Brig once more. You
are free.

